0238 sunfish: CA display/render-server threads on the A76 cores, kern.sweet_ui_bigcore (default 1),
sweetuibig=0 off (ios-redfin 1041, MIT)

v2 (2026-10-30, after the kernel114 reset "ub1"): xnu commits 0d04fcd + the v2 commit on top, as one diff.
- choose_processor no longer printf()s (sweet_ui_first_use removed): lock-free counters, read via
  sysctl kern.sweet_ui_idle, kern.sweet_ui_preempt, kern.sweet_ui_first ("tid T cpu C idle|preempt" or "none").
- sweetuibig is parsed only in thread context (sysctl, bsd_setthreadname); choose_processor reads the int
  (-1/unset = off).
- RT threads (sched_pri >= BASEPRI_RTQUEUES) only take an idle big core; preempt path is non-RT only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
